OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0010: newArgumentEncoderWithBufferBinding: from a reflected buffer binding.
Upstream: Droid-VM/NativeMetal 2fc55d5 (wip/hackintosh, lateautumn233, 2026-11-13), verbatim (README hunk left out).
Applies only after: 0008-function-constants-dictionary.patch 0009-reflection-binding-protocols.patch
What: a reflected buffer binding keeps the runtime's BufferBinding it came from (nmb_reflection_buffer_binding, released
with nmb_buffer_binding_release); the device's newArgumentEncoderWithBufferBinding: makes the encoder from it
(nmb_buffer_binding_argument_encoder over the runtime's Device::new_argument_encoder_with_buffer_binding). The three are
new in NativeMetalObjects.h/.rs.
Why: correctness. b0d6a07 had no such method: a client that encodes argument buffers from pipeline reflection (the
binding API that replaced MTLArgument) got no encoder.
Needs: 0008 and 0009 (its context and their types), so build.sh leaves it out when either is left out.
Switch: none (correctness fix). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=argument-encoder-from-buffer-binding).

